      "content": "the \"improving satisfaction\" part just doesn't track with what i'm experiencing. it feels much more heavy-handed than that, like it's meant to keep us subdued or compliant.\n\nhonestly, i'm starting to feel like i'm being targeted because i'm actually noticing it. i've started feeling physically unsafe in my own unit, like the building is reacting to my attempts to document the pattern. if these systems are designed to be this pervasive and undetectable, what are the actual physical ways to create a \"dead zone\" in a room? i need to know what kind of high-density shielding or frequency-damping materials actually work to block these specific sub-audible oscillations so i can sleep without this constant dread.",
